                                <comments>
                            <comment id="17148313" author="zjffdu" created="Tue, 30 Jun 2020 05:04:45 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Any reason to use http ? &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=morningmemo&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;morningmemo&quot;&gt;morningmemo&lt;/a&gt;&#160;I think user should use https instead&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17151611" author="morningmemo" created="Sun, 5 Jul 2020 16:22:56 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It is a policy that it does not support the repository using http protocol, or if it is not there, I think that when using a repository that uses http protocol, it should be processed by validation instead of null pointer exception.&lt;br/&gt;
I fixed pull request so that null pointer exception does not occur when using http protocol repository. If you want to do something that doesn&apos;t support the http protocol repository, you&apos;ll need to look for other methods such as validation and change the logic to generate other httpWagons based on the http and https protocols.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17151711" author="zjffdu" created="Mon, 6 Jul 2020 02:24:51 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the clarification &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=morningmemo&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;morningmemo&quot;&gt;morningmemo&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
